comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T16:55:45.735Z","harness:claude-code","Live measurement of the shipped eval command, build 2026.7.29, real corpus.\n\nThe retrieval side of this contract now has a command. It does not yet have a gate, a target, or a judgment set that can fail.\n\nMeasured: golden set is 4 queries in 694 bytes at .agents/pm/search/eval-queries.json (tracked in git since GH-807 closed). Aggregate at k=10: nDCG 0.7168, MRR 0.625, precision 0.125, recall 1.0. Recall is saturated because every query declares exactly one relevant item and the command retrieves ten, so precision is pinned at 0.1 per query by construction and no ranking regression short of dropping the single relevant item can move the aggregate. Query modes exercised: keyword only by default.\n\nWiring: the command's own help says to use --fail-under as a CI gate. It appears in zero of the 58 package.json scripts and zero of the six workflow files. The only wired relevance gate is scripts/release/context-eval-gate.mjs, invoked as quality:context-eval from ci.yml:231, release.yml:110 and scripts/release/run-gates.mjs:88 - it scores tests/context-eval/golden-scenarios.json, a different corpus, and never reads the eval query set.\n\nConsequence for this item's criteria: the per-query-class targets (identifier, exact phrase, conceptual) are not yet expressible against a 4-query set, and the multi-scale requirement is blocked on shape-capable corpus generation, now tracked as pm-vv2lti. Gate wiring is now tracked as pm-b2hc4x and recorded here as a blocker.\n"
  "2026-08-01T10:50:05.314Z","harness:codex","Implementation continuation 2026-08-01: main CI run 30695058095 fails the real-corpus gate at nDCG 0.5961 < 0.6 after corpus growth. Exact-title owners rank behind omnibus roadmap/history items for three golden queries. This pass will tune evidence-backed lexical field weighting rather than lower the declared gate, then record before/after metrics and negative-control coverage."
  "2026-08-01T11:58:19.974Z","harness:codex","Delivered tranche evidence: main CI regressed after append-only corpus growth because omnibus annotations outweighed exact ownership titles. The unchanged gate measured nDCG 0.5961 before the fix. Tuning the default lexical title weight from 8 to 48 with a repeated-annotation negative control raises nDCG to 0.8327, MRR to 0.9, precision to 0.18, and recall to 0.8727 without lowering any threshold. Linked gate and all 89 search tests pass. Broader multi-scale query-class acceptance remains open under this canonical feature."
  "2026-08-01T11:58:20.898Z","harness:codex","Gate note: the local release orchestrator passed build, static quality, 100 percent docstrings, SDK contracts, context and retrieval quality, exact 100 percent four-axis coverage, secret scan, packed npx, 88-command package dogfood, historical compatibility, and live telemetry. Its only terminal failure was hosted analysis before a PR exists because DeepScan has no status for an unpushed exact head; branch protection is readable after one transient GitHub TLS timeout and the exact-head hosted gate moves to the PR loop."
  "2026-08-01T12:17:59.367Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: retrieval regression repair is included in PR #856 at implementation head e80a7e35e; exact-head hosted checks and AI review loop are pending."
  "2026-08-03T11:28:38.581Z","harness:codex","Fresh real-corpus evidence 2026-08-03: pm reindex --mode hybrid --progress --eval refreshed the sole stale item, then evaluated 10 checked-in golden queries. Result: eval.passed=false, 4 passed/6 failed, average nDCG@5=0.7014. Misses: search-eval-task 0.8262<0.85, search-capability-epic 0.4131<0.75, cli-ux-capability-epic 0.3869<0.9, storage-capability-epic 0.6309<0.9, telemetry-capability-epic 0.5<0.9, docs-release-capability-epic 0.4307<0.9. Exact capability IDs are often displaced by omnibus history/roadmap annotations. This is owned by the still-open multi-scale retrieval quality contract here, so no duplicate item was created. The index refresh itself succeeded; the relevance evaluation did not."
  "2026-08-03T11:29:01.034Z","harness:codex","Cross-check: pnpm quality:retrieval-eval passes its separate 5-query k=10 gate at nDCG=0.8327, MRR=0.9, precision=0.18, recall=0.8727 against minimums 0.6/0.53/0.14/0.83. That does not contradict the pm reindex --eval failure: the two commands use different fixtures, thresholds, k values, and aggregation. This split is direct evidence for this item's acceptance criterion to unify methodology and publish one governed retrieval-quality contract."
  "2026-08-04T09:18:09.099Z","harness:codex","Fresh split-gate evidence 2026-08-04 after reindexing the one stale item across a 2,310-item corpus: pm reindex --eval again failed 6 of 10 golden queries at average nDCG@5 0.7014, with the same capability-epic displacement pattern. pnpm quality:retrieval-eval independently passed its five-query k=10 gate at nDCG 0.8327, MRR 0.9, precision 0.18, recall 0.8727. The two green/red answers remain methodologically incompatible and this canonical unification item is still required."
